<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Rewriting question in index form</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Rewrite each equation in index form by filling in the three boxes.</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(\log_{{@a@}} {@b@} = {@n@}\)</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]]<sup>[[input:ans2]]</sup> \(=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \(\log_{10} {@float(10^(-k))@} = -{@k@}\). A decimal or a fraction is fine.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]]<sup>[[input:ans5]]</sup> \(=\) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans4]] [[validation:ans5]] [[validation:ans6]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>A logarithm is an exponent:</p>
\[ \log_a b = n \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad a^n = b. \]
<p>The base of the logarithm is the base of the power, the value of the logarithm is the exponent, and the number inside the logarithm is the result.</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(\log_{{@a@}} {@b@} = {@n@} \;\Longleftrightarrow\; {@a@}^{@n@} = {@b@}\).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \(\log_{10} {@float(10^(-k))@} = -{@k@} \;\Longleftrightarrow\; 10^{-{@k@}} = {@float(10^(-k))@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
